WEBVTT

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.500
The B-rep model specifies the target geometry.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:15.000
The simulation starts from stock material.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:23.000
Each operation removes material along a toolpath.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:31.000
CNCGEN links planning and toolpaths through shared manufacturing objects.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:38.000
Earlier cuts change the material available to later steps.

00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:42.267
The updated stock records the effects of successive cuts.

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:46.267
The first case ends with the simulated workpiece.

00:00:46.267 --> 00:00:49.267
The second case combines a pocket, edges, and holes.

00:00:49.267 --> 00:00:57.533
Cutting starts at the edge of the second part.

00:00:57.533 --> 00:01:05.533
The readout identifies the current operation and tool.

00:01:05.533 --> 00:01:13.533
The evolving stock preserves the effects of preceding cuts.

00:01:13.533 --> 00:01:21.033
Each new cut acts on the stock left by earlier operations.

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:30.033
The cutter traces the central pocket as the stock is updated.

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:37.033
The sequence continues with the corner features.

00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:42.767
Further cuts form the corner holes.

00:01:42.767 --> 00:01:46.267
The second case ends with its final simulated geometry.
